<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Central Bank lowers mini-band on real.</title>
<headline>Brazil Central Bank lowers mini-band on real.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank lowered its mini-band on the real currency by buying dollars at 1.0710 reais per dollar and selling at 1.0760 in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>The previous mini-band was set May 30 between 1.0700 and 1.0750 reais per dollar.</p>
<p>Today's auction is the first time this month the bank has nudged the mini-band lower and represents a 0.09 percent decline from the previous mini-band.</p>
<p>In the last six months the Central Bank has lowered the mini-band by 0.57 to 0.63 percent each month.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
